From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: a frame the vsync queue skips last goes on the layer at the next tick

What: the vsync tick's trims (the quarter-second one, OMACVM_GL_TRIM=quarter, and the
once-a-second one) skip the frame left over after a tick, also when it is the only
one queued, which makes it the guest's newest. Such a frame now waits in
present_pend, with or without the tiled present, and the next tick that finds
nothing queued puts it on the layer. A frame that comes before that tick takes it
over, as before, so the trim still saves its refresh. While a frame waits there,
the tick does not end the link.
Why: nothing showed that frame. The tiled present parked it in present_pend for
the guest's next frame, and without the tiled present the tick dropped it. Its
draw had cleared gl_dirty, so present_bh asked for no present: at the end of a
scroll that a trim cut off, the window stayed one frame behind until the guest
drew again.
Upstream: OmacVM only (the present code is ours).
Test: app/runtime/Tests/display/test-present-skip.sh runs the queue's own code: a
scroll of drawn frames to the quarter-second trim, with the tiled present on and
off, with and without a frame after it, and a first tick a second late
(--self-test: it fails on the code without this patch).
Applies after omacvm-cocoa-present-tiles.patch and qemu-cocoa-gl-present-trim.patch,
before omacvm-cocoa-no-app-nap.patch.
diff --git a/ui/cocoa.m b/ui/cocoa.m
index 6218ad7..62a9861 100644
--- a/ui/cocoa.m
+++ b/ui/cocoa.m
@@ -11228,16 +11228,16 @@ static void present_frame_absorb(PresentFrame *newer, PresentFrame *older)
 }
 
 /*
- * present_lock held: OLDER is skipped. With the tiled present its updates
- * go into NEXT (the frame after it), or, when none is queued yet, wait in
- * present_pend for the next frame that comes. Else it just goes.
+ * present_lock held: OLDER is skipped. Its updates go into NEXT (the frame
+ * after it; a whole one lets OLDER go), or, when none is queued yet, OLDER
+ * waits in present_pend: the next frame that comes takes it over (a tile
+ * frame may lie over it), or else the next tick shows it, as it is the
+ * guest's newest.
  */
 static PresentFrame present_pend;
 static void present_frame_skip(PresentFrame *older, PresentFrame *next)
 {
-    if (present_tiles_on <= 0) {
-        present_frame_put(older);
-    } else if (next) {
+    if (next) {
         present_frame_absorb(next, older);
     } else {
         present_frame_absorb(older, &present_pend);
@@ -11692,6 +11692,11 @@ static bool cocoa_gl_present_vsync(double T)
     }
     present_sync.win_ticks++;
     present_sync.ticks++;
+    /* OmacVM: a frame skipped at the last tick that no newer one took over: it goes now. */
+    if (!present_sync.queued && (present_pend.surf || present_pend.pt)) {
+        present_sync.queue[present_sync.queued++] = present_pend;
+        present_pend = (PresentFrame){ 0 };
+    }
     if (present_sync.queued) {
         /*
          * Input is coming: frames that wait behind a newer one are old news
@@ -11785,8 +11790,9 @@ static bool cocoa_gl_present_vsync(double T)
         present_sync.merge =
             present_sync.win_flushes > present_sync.win_ticks * 5 / 4;
         if (!present_fixed && present_sync.win_gap2 >= PRESENT_CLOSE_S &&
-            !present_sync.queued && !present_sync.inflight) {
-            /* Frames came one at a time for a second: no link. */
+            !present_sync.queued && !present_sync.inflight &&
+            !present_pend.surf && !present_pend.pt) {
+            /* Frames came one at a time for a second: no link, once no frame waits for a tick. */
             present_sync.linked = false;
             present_sync.close_frames = 0;
             present_sync.merge = false;
